We can use the formulas in 1 and 2 to prove that the curve of 6cosΘ is a circle. 
The polar equation r = 6cosΘ that defines the curve requires a little ingenuity to convert to the corresponding Cartesian equation. 
The trick is to multiply both sides of the equation by r. 
Doing so, we obtain

			r² = 6r cosΘ

Now 1 and 2 immediaely give

			x² + y² = 6x

We complete the square in x to find that this equation can be rewritten as 

			(x - 3)² + y² = 9

which is indeed a circle of radius 3 with center at (3,0)
